> keybindings

The same as esc

```json
    {
        "key": "esc",
        "command": "workbench.action.quickOpen",
        "when": "!terminalFocus",
    },
    {
        "key": "esc",
        "command": "-workbench.action.quickOpen",
    },
```

@FreeSamples00 I got this PR, it should also fix things, and updates the docs to explain that using `agent.tools` field just represents the "allow" or "deny" permissions. But with this PR if you have any permissions set at the root layer of your config they get added in. But if you have `false` it just takes it as `deny` automatically.

**Update**
Spoke with someone on the team, they said that yes using tools is deprecated but they left it to work to support old configs, and its best to use permissions. Just like I said previously using true in tools is just like `"*": "allow"` for a tool and false is `"*": "deny"`. Ignoring permissions you set above.
